    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Radiation is the transfer of heat through space without needing any material, like sunlight reaching Earth. Dark surfaces absorb more radiation than light surfaces.\nThe Sun's heat drives the water cycle: water evaporates, forms clouds by condensation and falls as rain, snow or hail.\nSome rainwater seeps into the ground and becomes groundwater, which fills wells and borewells."
    }
